    "label": {
      "en": "Each 0.5 share higher threshold for reduced rate"
    },
    "short_label": {
      "en": "$tscxc_thres4"
    },
    "description": {
      "en": "This is the incremental RFR (reference tax income) amount — 4,474 EUR for 2025 — added per additional 0.5 family-quotient share above the base of 1 share, used to raise the CSG reduced-rate threshold for larger tax households when determining CSG liability on pension income. It is used in policy tinty_fr in the ArithOp that 'calculates the applicable threshold for reduced rate for pensions', alongside the base 1-share threshold $tscxc_thres3."
    },
    "explanation": {
      "en": "EUROMOD function group: Parameters for determining net taxable income (RNI)"
    },
